From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: pin QSA sparse attention to four warps

The 0.32 config table selects a single-warp split-k for 25-32 programs.
On MUSA that reduction leaves the attention output unnormalized, so every
prompt longer than 24 tokens produced garbage logits. Restore the 0.28
override that always runs four warps.
---
 vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
index 401048e02c..00d303af6f 100644
--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
@@ -588,6 +588,10 @@ def _select_config(
     num_tiles = triton.cdiv(num_columns, BLOCK_N)
     # Never more splits than tiles, never empty.
     num_splits = min(target_splits, num_tiles)
+    if current_platform.is_musa():
+        # Single-warp split-k reductions yield unnormalized attention outputs
+        # on MUSA; keep four warps as in the 0.28 enablement.
+        num_warps = 4
     return BLOCK_N, num_warps, num_tiles, num_splits
 
 
